# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
node_modules/

# Secrets. Real values only ever live here, never in a tracked OS file.
.env*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch. Never tracked, in the template or in a clone.
#
# .deliverables/ is local-only working scratch. It is NOT the deliverables
# folder. Only its README is tracked, and that README exists to say so.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.deliverables/*
!.deliverables/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and it should stay that way:
#
#   00-deliverables/   tracked work. Deliverables have to be reviewable,
#                      linkable from 00-tasks.md, and present in a fresh
#                      clone. That is the whole point of the folder.
#   00-tasks.md        the company-wide index over those deliverables.
#   00-templates/      reusable formats, shared across the company.
#   01-sops/           shipped framework: cross-agent conventions.
#   03-skills/         shipped framework: bootstrap-company, add-new-agent.
#
#   01-identity/       your OS, written by bootstrap. The template ships
#   02-context/        without these because the files are not in the repo,
#   04-memory/         not because anything ignores them. Once bootstrap
#   05-connections/    writes them, commit them. An untracked OS cannot be
#   06-agents/         reviewed, cannot be recovered, and does not follow you
#                      to a second machine, and git status will look clean the
#                      whole time.
#
# Secrets are the exception, and they are already handled above: real values
# live in a .env* file, all of which are ignored. Files in 05-connections/
# point at where credentials live and never hold the values themselves, so
# they are safe to track. See 03-skills/bootstrap-company/SKILL.md, phase 5.3.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
